  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given integers NNN, KKK and an array BBB of length NNN.\n\nCount the number of arrays AAA, also of length NNN, which satisfy the following conditions:\n\n\n1≤Ai≤K1 \\le A_i \\le K1≤Ai​≤K\nThe lexicographically largest†^{\\dagger}† subsequence‡^{\\ddagger}‡ of A[1,i]A[1, i]A[1,i] has a length of BiB_iBi​.\n\nA[1,i]A[1, i]A[1,i] represents the prefix of the array containing iii elements, i.e. [A1,A2,…,Ai][A_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_i][A1​,A2​,…,Ai​].\nSince the answer may be large, output it modulo 998244353998244353998244353.\n\n†^{\\dagger}† A sequence XXX is said to be lexicographically larger than YYY if either of the following conditions holds:\n\n\nYYY is a prefix of XXX but X≠YX \\ne YX=Y.\nThe first index iii where Xi≠YiX_i \\ne Y_iXi​=Yi​ satisfies Xi&gt;YiX_i &gt; Y_iXi​&gt;Yi​.\n‡^{\\ddagger}‡ A sequence XXX is a subsequence of YYY if it is possible to obtain YYY by deleting any number (possibly zero) of elements from YYY without changing the order of the remaining elements.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains 222 integers - NNN and KKK.\nThe second line contains NNN integers - B1,B2,…,BNB_1, B_2, \\ldots, B_NB1​,B2​,…,BN​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line the number of valid arrays AAA modulo 998244353998244353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\le T \\le 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N,K≤30001 \\le N, K \\le 30001≤N,K≤3000",
      "1≤Bi≤i1 \\le B_i \\le i1≤Bi​≤i",
      "Both the sum of NNN and the sum of KKK over all tests does not exceed 300030003000."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
