      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "5\n1 1000\n1\n2 2\n1 2\n2 2\n1 1\n5 4\n1 1 3 3 3\n7 6\n1 2 1 2 2 3 4",
        "output": "1000\n3\n1\n0\n4518",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest Case 1 : All arrays of length 111 with 1≤A1≤10001 \\le A_1 \\le 10001≤A1​≤1000 is valid. There are 100010001000 such arrays.\nTest Case 2 : The valid arrays are [2,1],[1,1],[2,2][2, 1], [1, 1], [2, 2][2,1],[1,1],[2,2]. However, [1,2][1, 2][1,2] is not valid because for the prefix of length 222, the lexicographically largest subsequence is [2][2][2] which has length 111.\nTest Case 3 : The only valid array is [1,2][1, 2][1,2]."
      }
